  "finalAnswerPreview": "## Determination\\n\\n**The integration should expect a typed `InvalidCursorError` from `@ordarium/core` — an `OrdariumError` whose `code` is the string `\\\"INVALID_CURSOR\\\"` — raised fail-closed. It should *not* expect (or classify on) numeric code **27**.**\\n\\nIts message is literally *\\\"The change cursor is not a valid durable position; refusing to guess a resume point\\\"* (`node_modules/@ordarium/core/dist/src/errors.js:161-165`, declared at `errors.d.ts:92-100`).\\n\\n## What \\\"stored observation cursor\\\" is here\\n\\nThe workspace's Ordarium integration surface is the management-state store (`OrdariumStateStore`, obtained via `createPalimpsestEffects` → `createStateStore({ runtime })`, `src/effects/runtime.ts:113`). The \\\"observation\\\" surface is the revisioned **state change feed**:\\n\\n- `StateChangeFeed.changes(filter?, cursor?)` is documented as *\\\"Incremental observation of committed state revisions after a durable position\\\"* (`@ordarium/core/dist/src/types.d.ts:205-215`, `state.d.ts:26-30`).\\n- `StateChangePage.cursor` is *\\\"opaque, filter-independent durable position\\\"* — a value a consumer stores and hands back later (`types.d.ts:168-178`).\\n\\nSo a \\\"stored observation cursor",
